[{"text":"SIS[p] can be used as input for 3-dimensional \\sigma^{\\mu } p_{\\mu } with 4-dimensional Lorentz vector \\(p\\) and is transformed into PauliSigma[Momentum[p]] by FeynCalcInternal.","anchor":"sis"},{"text":"Overview, PauliSigma, SISD.","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"SIS[p]","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\sigma }\\cdot \\overline{p}\\]","anchor":"cb1-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"SIS[p] // FCI // StandardForm (*PauliSigma[Momentum[p]]*)","anchor":"cb2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"SIS[p, q, r, s]","anchor":"cb3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left(\\bar{\\sigma }\\cdot \\overline{p}\\right).\\left(\\bar{\\sigma }\\cdot \\overline{q}\\right).\\left(\\bar{\\sigma }\\cdot \\overline{r}\\right).\\left(\\bar{\\sigma }\\cdot \\overline{s}\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb3-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"SIS[p, q, r, s] // StandardForm (*SIS[p] . SIS[q] . SIS[r] . SIS[s]*)","anchor":"cb4","section":"Examples"},{"text":"SIS[q] . (SIS[p] + m) . SIS[q]","anchor":"cb5","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left(\\bar{\\sigma }\\cdot \\overline{q}\\right).\\left(\\bar{\\sigma }\\cdot \\overline{p}+m\\right).\\left(\\bar{\\sigma }\\cdot \\overline{q}\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb5-1","section":"Examples"}]